  "id": "assisted-death",
  "term": "assisted death",
  "definition": "Assisted death refers to a practice in which a physician helps bring about a person’s death, usually in the context of severe suffering and a voluntary wish to die. In this packet, it is discussed as a legally and ethically disputed issue, especially when the suffering is linked to psychiatric disorder rather than physical illness.",
